    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "Both tests pass and the full build (including the frontend typecheck/build and Maven compile) completed with no errors.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the invoice lifecycle **DRAFT \u2192 SENT \u2192 PAID** as a small, additive full-stack change:\n\n**Database** (`src/main/resources/db/migration/V11__invoice_draft_default.sql`)\n- New migration changing the `invoice.status` default to `'DRAFT'` so freshly created invoices start as drafts. The existing `VARCHAR(16)` column already holds the new status values.\n\n**Server** (OfficeFloor REST on Spring Boot)\n- New endpoint `POST /api/invoices/send` \u2014 new YAML (`invoices/send.POST.yml`) + logic class `InvoiceSend` + request body `SendInvoice`. It requires the invoice to still be a `DRAFT`, flips it to `SENT`, and records the audit line `INVOICE_SENT id=<id> amount=<amount>` via the injected `Audit` service.\n- `InvoicePay` now rejects payment unless the invoice is `SENT` (\"payment only allowed once sent\").\n- `InvoicesPost` now creates invoices as `DRAFT` instead of `UNPAID`.\n\n**Front-end** (`features/invoices/InvoicesPanel.tsx`, the invoices feature's own panel)\n- Added a `send` mutation (POST + `invalidateQueries(['invoices'])`) and a per-row **Send** button (`invoice-send-<id>`) shown only when status is `DRAFT`.\n- Gated the existing **Mark paid** button (`invoice-pay-<id>`) to appear only when status is `SENT`, so a draft has no pay control until it's been sent.\n\nThe status is surfaced through the existing `invoice-status` testid, and audited behaviour goes through the `Audit` service exactly as the spec's `INVOICE_SENT id=1 amount=100.00` record expects.",
